# Tests

Mirror the code: `tests/models/test_<model>.py`, `tests/services/test_<service>.py`, `tests/selectors/test_<selector>.py`. Name the class `<Name>Tests`. Model validation tests call `full_clean` and do not need the database. Service tests hit the database and mock anything outside the project. Use factories once `factory_boy` is introduced. Until then, `Model.objects.create` or another service is fine.

```python
# ❌ BAD — validation is asserted through the database
class TestUser(TestCase):
    def test_email(self):
        User.objects.create(email="Not-Lower@example.com")

# ✅ GOOD
class UserTests(SimpleTestCase):
    def test_clean_rejects_mixed_case_email(self):
        user = User(email="Not-Lower@example.com")
        with self.assertRaises(ValidationError):
            user.full_clean()
```
